    <section class="section about" id="about">
      <div class="container about-layout">
        <div class="fade-up"><div class="section-label">01 / Who we are</div><h2 style="font:700 clamp(36px,4vw,61px)/1.18 Manrope;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:0">Building the next generation of <span style="color:#10a69e">intelligent machines.</span></h2></div>
        <div class="fade-up"><p class="about-description">RoMeCoLa — the Robotics, Mechanics, and Control Laboratory — conducts interdisciplinary research across robot design, dynamics and control, machine learning, and embodied intelligence. Our work bridges foundational methods with robotic systems operating in challenging environments.</p><p class="about-description">We study how robots can understand their surroundings, learn from interaction, and execute complex tasks with greater adaptability, autonomy, and reliability.</p><div class="about-tags"><span class="about-tag">Robot Design</span><span class="about-tag">Embodied AI</span><span class="about-tag">World Models</span><span class="about-tag">Reinforcement Learning</span><span class="about-tag">Mobile Manipulation</span></div><div class="about-graphic"><div class="about-metric"><strong>04</strong><small>Core research<br>themes</small></div><div class="about-metric"><strong>13</strong><small>Research project<br>directions</small></div><div class="about-metric"><strong>01</strong><small>Connected research<br>vision</small></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section research" id="research">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading fade-up"><div><div class="section-label">02 / Research</div><h2>Explore the frontiers<br>of physical AI.</h2></div><p class="section-desc">Our research spans the full robotics stack, from bio-inspired mechanisms and perception to learning, planning, control, and real-world autonomy.</p></div>
        <div class="pillar-grid fade-up"><div class="pillar"><div class="pillar-number">THEME 01</div><div class="pillar-symbol">◎</div><h3>Embodied AI &<br>Robot Learning</h3><p>World models, VLA policies, reinforcement learning, and intelligent manipulation.</p></div><div class="pillar"><div class="pillar-number">THEME 02</div><div class="pillar-symbol">◇</div><h3>Legged &<br>Collaborative Robotics</h3><p>Autonomy, whole-body motion, navigation, and multi-robot collaboration.</p></div><div class="pillar"><div class="pillar-number">THEME 03</div><div class="pillar-symbol">✳</div><h3>Bio-inspired &<br>Aerial Robotics</h3><p>Flapping-wing flight, agile navigation, and biologically inspired machines.</p></div><div class="pillar"><div class="pillar-number">THEME 04</div><div class="pillar-symbol">⌁</div><h3>Intelligent<br>Industrial Automation</h3><p>Learning-based systems for complex, practical industrial environments.</p></div></div>
        <div class="research-intro fade-up"><h3>Research projects <span style="font-weight:400;color:#9baab2">/ 13</span></h3><span class="small-note">An open view of our research portfolio ↓</span></div>
        <div class="project-grid" id="projectsGrid" aria-label="All research projects"></div>
        <div class="research-outro"><span>From foundational machine intelligence to <strong>real-world robotic embodiment.</strong></span><span>Interested in collaborating? <a href="mailto:tzou@mun.ca" style="color:#068f86;font-weight:800">Get in touch ↗</a></span></div>
      </div>
